      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Technical Incident Summary: CFM56-7B Engine Anomaly During Pre-Flight Check**\n\nDuring a standard pre-flight engine inspection, a discrepancy was noted with the CFM56-7B engine. The technician recorded a slight but unusual vibration in the N1 shaft as the engine underwent startup procedures. Additionally, a transient elevated exhaust gas temperature (EGT) peak of 15 degrees above standard parameters was observed, persisting for approximately three seconds. Despite these anomalies, oil pressure remained steady within expected operational thresholds, and leaks were not visibly apparent. An unexplained faint grinding noise was captured emanating from the vicinity of the fan case. Given these observations, a further in-depth mechanical examination is advised to ascertain the cause of these symptoms and implement necessary remedial actions.",
      "source": "target",
