      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The reevaluated Technical Incident Summary accounting for Maintenance Error Codes is as follows:\n\nDuring the routine pre-flight inspection, the CFM56-7B's performance was belying the expected norms due to an evident deviation. Firstly, the recorded vibration of the N1 shaft (VIB-09) registered during the engine's initial RPM phase, suggesting a potential issue with the shaft brace or flywheel imbalance. Concurrently, a temporary EGT spike was identified, coded as EGT-772, which exceeds the established normal operational envelope by approximately 15 degrees for a duration of three seconds. The exhaust gas temperature subsequently reverted to its standard range, indicating a potentially ephemeral and non-permanent condition. Oil pressure diagnostics yielded no signal of malfunction, and its stability within the safe zone indicates that it remained within the green arc despite the shaft's anomalous behavior. Noise diagnostics detected an extraneous auditory anomaly (MEC-44), characterized as a faint grinding emanating from the fan section, which suggests possible contamination or misalignment instances within the vicinity. These findings necessitate an immediate and exhaustive mechanical analysis of the affected components to rectify any identified malfunctions or obstructions potentially compromising the aircraft's safety.",
      "source": "target",
